From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:30:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): autodetect never picks a server-side-only search
 provider

The openai-native web provider only declares OpenAI's server-side web_search tool on the Codex Responses transport. Autodetect picked it whenever OpenAI or Codex credentials existed, so every client-side web_search call failed and fell back to the keyless tier. A provider now declares runs_client_side() (False for openai-native); the autodetect ladder and the registry availability walk skip it, and a failed call on it is not rescued by the keyless ring, so an explicit pin on another transport returns its one-line error. The pin still drives the Codex swap.
